// Dialog :
"P2340210907" "I have received the results of the divination from Tarixus! The seals aren't meant to bind the Wailers to the Golden Giza - they're there to keep the demons out of Babylon! Something the demons want is inside the Golden Giza, and it's only the seals that are keeping them out. If the seals break, it means that St. Martial is going to be overrun with demons, and we're ALL dead."
// RandomFameString :
"P3637866758" "I heard {VillainName} was busting some demon heads with Hardcase on St. Martial!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission_6 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P1875755441" "So someone wants to keep the Wailer demons out of Babylon, eh? I'd like to find out who. I found out where the property records for Babylon are being kept - this may provide us a link to whoever financed the building of the Golden Giza. <A HREF={ACCEPT}>Raid the office where the property records are being kept.</A>"
// AcceptString :
"P905522002" "Steal Babylon property records"
// SendOffString :
"P2038948362" "You might have to deal with some private security there. A lot of money flows around St. Martial, so you can be sure these guys are top-notch."
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P2719815464" "You steal those records yet? Get on that!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P4132996023" "The office smells of polish and carpet cleaner."

